  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "A CRISPR-based benchmark of causal GRN inference appears alongside preprints modelling assay and label noise or topological bias in biomedical prediction.",
  "synthesis": "Only one item directly benchmarks causal network inference: a published comparison of interventional causal structure learning algorithms on synthetic and CRISPR perturbation data for gene regulatory network inference. The remaining items are heterogeneous predictive-modelling studies that share a concern with data quality and bias rather than causal discovery. DeepCINET and siGMA model assay noise and label noise or heterogeneity, the latter via aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty. The Inverse Node Frequency preprint reduces hub bias in knowledge-graph metapath features for target-adverse event prediction. Further items apply spatial transcriptomic correlation to anticancer drug prediction and hybrid quantum machine learning to KCNQ missense pathogenicity. The common thread is evaluating and correcting systematic distortions in biological data, with the causal benchmark providing the clearest test of method performance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
